Robot 1 (ducks): collect all five in one go with a low tray or hopper, then do a single loop through the five zones and release one duck per zone with a servo gate. One loop beats five round trips on both time and reliability. Budget about 20 s to collect and 40 to 50 s for the loop, re-aligning on the tape lines or the PVC walls before each drop. With the time left, sweep the 15 cluster poms on the left half of the line off the tape (15 base points, 75 effective) into a zone that will not get the singles.

Robot 2 (points), in this order:

Cups: flip both upright (20 each) and nudge them off the tape (+1 each). Nesting is also 20 but needs a carry, only worth it if the rules let a nested pair count as two uprights plus nested (60).
Mystery red pom alone on the platform (50). The big duck has to leave the platform first: push it off (it earns +1 on the floor; carry it to Botguy’s start later for 15 if time remains).
The five single poms on the right half of the line are already one of each color. Sweep them into a pile and push the pile into one zone: 25 plus 5 base. Keep them away from the cluster poms, one duplicate color drops the zone from 25 to about 3.
The pickleball on the bottom border at the center line is right next to the platform: knock it off the post and push it under (7). The other three balls are far away and roll unpredictably, chase them only with spare seconds.
Big duck to Botguy’s start, Botguy onto the platform, rings on bottle necks: 15 each, all slow or needing a lift. Rings are the hardest (lift over an 8 inch post, then drop over a neck). Fallback: drop a ring touching a bottle for 3.
